                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "um351":</h3><p><b>UM351</b> is the model name of a microphone output transformer designed by AMI for use in restoration of vintage Gefell microphones such as the <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Neumann/CMV-563">CMV563</a> and <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Neumann/UM-57">UM57</a>. </p><p>The transformer, which has no faradaic shield, is also found in the modern Gefell UM75.</p><p>See Oliver Archut&#8217;s <a href="http://www.tab-funkenwerk.com/id72.html">history of the UM351 transformer</a>.</p>
